# BusyBox init's table, in the format <id>:<runlevels>:<action>:<process>. The system has no
# runlevels, so the runlevels field is empty.
#
# The kernel mounts devtmpfs on /dev before init starts, so /dev is not mounted here. The system has
# no fstab: the file systems are mounted here, by name.
#
# init runs a process through /bin/sh only when its command has shell characters, and none of these
# has any.

# The file systems that the kernel does not mount: its two interfaces, and the run-time directory.
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t tmpfs tmpfs /run

# The console: the virtio console, hvc0, which the platform names as its CONSOLE. -L sets CLOCAL,
# as a virtual console has no carrier to detect. The baud rate 0 keeps the terminal's own.
hvc0::respawn:/sbin/getty -L 0 hvc0

# Run at poweroff, before init kills the remaining processes. The file systems are unmounted, or
# remounted read-only where they are busy, such as the root file system under the shell.
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
